    c.print("# together, where the last definition of a name is the one that runs — so these\n");
    c.print("# blocks must stay byte-identical (tools/completions/selftest.sh checks it).\n");
    c.print("#\n");
    c.print("# COMP_WORDBREAKS contains '=', so bash hands \"--target=lin\" to us as the three\n");
    c.print("# words \"--target\" \"=\" \"lin\". Every long option that takes its value after an\n");
    c.print("# '=' was therefore invisible to a `case \"$cur\" in --target=*)` test — it never\n");
    c.print("# matched, and TAB fell through to plain file completion.\n");
    c.print("#\n");
    c.print("# __caustic_comp_init sets, for the caller:\n");
    c.print("#   cur   the text readline will replace — it does NOT carry the \"--opt=\"\n");
